---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE } from "../lib/site";
---

<Base
  title="How a receipt works"
  description="Every Can’t Explain entry needs a claim, an original source, and a file in git. Here is what that means."
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: "Home", href: "/" },
    { name: "Method", href: "/method" },
  ]}
>
  <div class="wrap wrap-narrow section">
    <p class="eyebrow">Method</p>
    <h1>How a receipt works</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      If you cannot open the source, and you cannot open the file, it is not in the hall.
      Humour is allowed. Invented quotes are not.
    </p>

    <h2>The four fields that matter</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <strong>Claim</strong> — quoted, or marked as a paraphrase. One accusation per card.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Source</strong> — the original public URL and its date. A quote-tweet of a
        screenshot is not original enough.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Evidence</strong> — a capture committed under
        <code>evidence/</code> in
        <a href={SITE.repo}>{SITE.repo.replace("https://", "")}</a>. The immutable
        timestamp is the git commit, not a date we typed.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Caption</strong> — one or two observational sentences. If it still works
        after you delete the source, it was a dunk. We spike dunks.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Git as the clock</h2>
    <p>
      Screenshots can be edited. Headlines can move. A file in this repository has an
      author, a hash, and a time. We do not rewrite a capture in place to make it tidier
      — we add another file and say so. Archive.org links are a spare key, not the lock.
    </p>

    <h2>What gets in</h2>
    <p>
      Low evidence, high emotion. The tell is usually the missing step: control asserted
      without a mechanism, guilt by a nearby name, certainty with the footnote still
      “to come”. Launch themes are Hanson Derangement Syndrome, “Gina’s Puppet”, and “No
      Evidence Required”. The hall is open to any figure who attracts the same shape of
      claim.
    </p>

    <h2>What does not</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Ordinary disagreement with a sourced argument.</li>
      <li>A second smear offered as a “receipt”.</li>
      <li>Private messages, hacked mail, or anything we cannot show you.</li>
      <li>AI-only publication. Models may draft. A human opens the URL.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      The owner adds cards with <code>npm run new</code>. The build fails if a published
      entry is missing its source or its file. See
      <a href="https://github.com/coldix/cantexplain/blob/main/docs/CONTENT-MODEL.md">the content model</a>.
      Limits of what a card means: <a href="/disclaimer">disclaimer</a>. Common questions:
      <a href="/faq">FAQ</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
